---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RecoveryLab from '../../labs/recovery/RecoveryLab.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Connection Recovery Lab | David Blumenau" description="Disconnect a recorded client stream and recover the actual completed answer. A controlled Claude Engine execution with inspectable timestamps and result receipts.">
  <main id="main" class="rl-page">
    <section class="rl-hero wrap" id="top"><a class="rl-back" href="/work/connected-agents/"><Icon name="arrow-left" /> Connected agents</a><div class="rl-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Engine room / A working outcome</p><h1>The window closes.<br /><em>The answer arrives.</em></h1></div><div><p>I built a stored-result path into Claude Engine so a broken client stream can collect the completed turn.</p><span class="rl-notice">An actual local execution, replayed here.</span></div></div></section>
    <div class="wrap"><RecoveryLab /></div>
    <section class="rl-recording wrap" aria-labelledby="rl-recording-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">Watch the original execution</p><h2 id="rl-recording-title">The connection<br /><em>really closed.</em></h2><p>A separate browser, the committed engine source and an isolated Redis instance. The screen freezes at 23 characters, while the engine finishes all 2,632. The result endpoint first returns 202, then returns the completed answer twice.</p><p class="rl-capture-note">Controlled local capture · fictional content · 14 October 2026. No production service, notification recipient or unrelated session was involved.</p></div><figure><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/media/recovery/disconnected.png" aria-label="Actual controlled client-disconnect and result-recovery recording" aria-describedby="rl-video-description"><source src="/media/recovery/execution.mp4" type="video/mp4" /><track kind="captions" src="/media/recovery/execution.vtt" srclang="en" label="English" default />Your browser does not support this video. <a href="/media/recovery/execution.mp4">Download the recording.</a></video><figcaption id="rl-video-description">A genuine continuous browser recording of the controlled run. The upper exhibit is a static replay of its recorded events. The engine process stays alive throughout.</figcaption></figure></section>
    <section class="rl-reading wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Why the answer survives</p><h2>Finishing the work is<br /><em>only half the job.</em></h2><p>The engine keeps collecting the turn after its client disconnects. Once the answer is complete, it stores the final text and ordered timeline in Redis. A result endpoint makes that completion available for later retrieval; idempotent reads let more than one client collect it.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work/connected-agents/">Read the connected agents story <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></a></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
